WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:09.920
I think that freedom everywhere,
anywhere, is love.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:15.520
Letting yourself be loved,
which is always risky.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.440
And loving, which is
maybe even riskier.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.560
I've been an monk here
at Pluscarden for 47 years.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.920
Prayer I suppose is the
greatest freedom of all,

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:45.840
because

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:48.760
it's a relationship,

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.360
it's a gift of God,

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:56.040
it's very mysterious I think.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:08.760
It's a gift and you just
accept what comes.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:16.080
Silence is an enabling thing.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:20.960
It frees you for

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:25.000
listening, for availability,

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:29.920
for avoiding imposing yourself.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.040
How often in speech
are we trying to do someone down

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:37.840
or demonstrate our superiority
or all of that.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.840
So, silence frees you
from those things.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:54.960
Most monks do all sorts of things.

00:01:55.960 --> 00:02:00.280
So you take your turn washing up,
peeling the spuds, cooking the lunch,

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:01.840
driving the car.

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:04.600
Many little jobs.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.520
Just like a family.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.680
Habere est Haberi,

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:21.480
which means, "What you possess,
possesses you."

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:26.760
The less you've got,
the more freedom you have.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:30.360
And that’s

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:36.520
a freedom which is quite hard
to acquire in some ways

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:40.320
because letting go of things
is detachment.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.760
It's difficult but it's essential
for freedom

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.560
because as our lives go on,

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:49.520
you have to let go of things.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:54.840
Maybe your memory, maybe your sight,
maybe your hearing, maybe mobility.

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.120
You've got to let them go.

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:03.200
Because one day,
you have to let go of your life -

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:06.360
the ultimate impoverishment.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:11.400
But that’s the only way to get
to the freedom of eternal life.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:33.560
It will be tough at times,
everybody's life is tough at times.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:38.200
But as they say, the retirement
benefits are out of this world.

